    "Fresh raw HTTP: Turbo 2.22/2.72s versus Max 2.61/2.34s. The earlier 17\u201353s portrait requests were not reproducible in this session. Do not conclude Turbo is inherently slower.",
    "Production SDK fal.run: Turbo 2.57s; Max 2.03s. Raw HTTP offers no demonstrated advantage. Queued Turbo 3.21s; observed IN_PROGRESS at 0.263s. Keep synchronous runtime calls.",
    "GPU denoising remained 0.42\u20130.86s. Fal marketing benchmark explicitly measures timings.inference, not complete user wait; preprocessing/encoding/network/queue time are not separately exposed here.",
    "No misconfiguration found: 480P, five seconds, prompt expansion disabled. SDK has retries, but earlier instrumented calls had a single HTTP 200. Provider load/startup variation is plausible, not proven.",
    "Lite PNG portraits 4.42\u20134.74s; JPEG 3.58\u20134.59s. PNG downloads 1.39\u20131.50s versus JPEG 0.63\u20130.71s; runtime forwards provider image URL immediately so local download is not the video critical path.",
    "Nano Banana 2 controls 9.78/35.80s. Only two photo samples; no production percentiles.",
    "The animated-glasses defect is a downstream video observation, not proof that Lite still images are unacceptable. Human A/B judgement takes precedence over automated quality scores."
  ],
  "decision": "Keep Turbo portrait routing and Nano Banana 2 runtime settings for now; present paired stills and animations for the user to judge. No automatic production swap based on this small latency sample.",
